Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 09:50:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 30/56] PROTOTYPE pco: take gl_FragCoord.xy from the pixel
 registers in pixel-rate transfer shaders

For internal shaders pco picks the pixel or sample position registers at
run time from the coverage mask (pck.cov, shift, test, select: six
instruction groups per component). A transfer shader that is not sample
rate runs on a single-sampled ISP (pvr_msaa_state() only leaves it
multisampled for sample-rate or iterated shaders, and iterated ones read
a varying), so the driver can say so: pco_fs_data.pixel_rate_pos.

With the previous patch the R8 copy shader goes from 31 instruction groups
to 5; a 1280x720 R8 upload takes 1.1 ms of GPU time instead of 2.6.

